# VIDEO_CARDS, with the profile defaults cleared first.
#
# The leading "-*" is load-bearing: without it the profile's own defaults
# (video_cards_nouveau, _vesa, _dummy, _radeon) survive and those drivers get
# built on every image, silently. Portage reports nothing about it.
#
# This is why the list lives here and not in make.conf: a make.conf assignment
# cannot clear profile defaults, only add to them.
# vc4 removed: it is the Raspberry Pi GPU driver and is masked in
# profiles/arch/base/use.mask, so it can never activate on amd64.
# nouveau (2026-10-01): the mesa side of the open NVIDIA driver, for the boot
# entry "open NVIDIA driver" -- the GPUs >=nvidia-drivers-595 dropped (Maxwell,
# Pascal) get 3D acceleration instead of llvmpipe. The kernel module is in-tree.
*/* VIDEO_CARDS: -* amdgpu d3d12 fbdev intel nouveau nvidia qxl radeonsi virgl virtualbox
